# Iteration 1 - Operations and contracts 

##1) System Operations:
- createTask(title, description?, priority, dueDate?, project?, tags?) -> taskId
- updateTask(taskId, title?, description?, priority?, dueDate?, project?, tags?) -> void
- completeTask(taskId) -> void
- cancelTask(taskId) -> void 
- viewTasks() -> List<Task> 
- createSubtask(taskId, title) -> subtaskId
- completeSubtask(taskId, subtaskId) -> void
- manageProject() -> void
- manageSubTask(taskId) -> void
- searchTask(query) -> List<Task>
- viewTaskActivity(taskId) -> List<Activity>
- recordTaskActivity(taskId, description) -> void(internal) 
- listTasks(type, value) -> List<Task>
- viewTasksDue(dueDate) -> List<Task>
- viewTaskRange(startDate, endDate) -> List<Task>

## Task Status:
A task can have one of the following statues:
- open
- cancelled
- completed
Open is the default 

Status transitions:
- open -> completed
- open -> cancelled

## Task Tag:
Tasks may be categroized using tags
Tags are user-defined keywords
- one task can have multiple tags
- one tag may be associated with multiple tasks

##2) Operation Contracts

### createTask(title, description?, priority, dueDate?, project?,tags?) -> taskId

Preconditions:
- title needs to be provided
- priority needs to be provided

Postconditions: 
- new task is created
- title is stored
- description is stored if provided
- due date is stored if provided
- priority is stored
- if tags are provided then the task is associated with theese tags
- task can have 0 or more tags
- creation date is automatically set
- status is set to open by default
- a unique taskId is returned
- if a project is not provided then the task belongs to no project by default
- recordTaskActivity(taskId, "task created") is exectued

### update(taskId, title?, description?, priority?, dueDate?, project?, tag?)

Postconditions:
- task already exists
- if tags provided/updated then the task-tag association should be updated accordingly
- title needs to be provided and non-empty

Postconditions:
- only provided attributes are updated
- recordTaskActivity(taskId, "task updated") is exectued

### cancelTask(taskId)

Preconditions:
- task already exists
- status is open

Postconditions:
- task status change to cancelled
- recordTaskActivity(taskId, "task cancelled") is executed

### viewTasks()

Preconditions:
- none

Postconditions:
- all stored tasks are displayed
- no data is modified

### searchTask(query)

Preconditions:
- query needs to be provided and non-empty

Postconditions:
- matching tasks are returned
- no data is modified

### createSubtask(taskId, title) -> subtaskId

Preconditions:
- parent task exists
- title is provided and non-empty

Postconditions:
- subtask is created
- subtask is associatyed with only one parent task
- subtask cannot exsit independently (composition)
- subtask status is set to open by default
- a unique subtask ID is returned

### completeSubtask(taskId, subtaskId) 

Preconditions:
- parent task exists
- subtask exists under that task
- subtask status is open

Postconditions:
- subtask status becomes completed
- parent task status is not modified automatically 

### manageProject()

Precondition:
- none

Postcondition:
- project information is managed within the system

### viewTaskActivity(taskId)

Preconditions:
- task already exists

Postconditions:
- activity history is displayed for the task in question
- no task data is modified

### recordTaskActivity(taskId, description)

Preconditions:
- task already exists
- description is provided

Postconditions:
- new activity entry is added to task history

### listTasks(type?, value?)

Preconditions:
- type should be either dueDate, priority, status, project or tag

Postconditions:
-tasks matching the filtering are displayed
- no task is modified

### viewTasksDue(dueDate?)

Preconditions:
- dueDate is provided

Postconditions:
- tasks with dueDate matching the input are displayed
- no data is modified

### viewTaskRange(startDate?, endDate?)

Preconditions:
-startDate and endDate are provided
- startDate <= endDate

Postconditions:
- tasks due within the range are displayed
- no data is modified







